---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="About B's Journal — a space for essays on biology, literature, religion, culture, and the human spirit."
>
  <article class="about">
    <header class="container about-header">
      <h1 class="about-title">About</h1>
    </header>

    <div class="container about-layout">
      <div class="about-content">
        <p>
          My name is Bhavya. For a while, my days were measured in roadmaps and sprint cycles —
          the language of product management, where everything is built to be shipped. I have
          since left that world for teaching, though I suspect I never really left the habit of
          asking why something works. Biology was where that habit began. It is still the ground
          I stand on: the discipline that taught me a body is a story told in cells, that a life
          is, before anything else, a system trying to persist.
        </p>
        <p>
          But systems alone never satisfied me. Somewhere in the reading that followed —
          literature, culture, the long unspooling of history — I began to see how deeply the
          human mind is not just a product of biology, but a shaper of it in return: of the
          cultures we build, the beliefs we inherit, the wars we wage and the peace we
          occasionally manage to keep. Mechanism gave me the how. Everything else, slowly, began
          to give me the why. This journal is my attempt to hold both at once, without asking
          either to explain away the other.
        </p>
        <p>
          Away from the writing desk, I am — perhaps unexpectedly — a gamer, which has taught me
          more about systems, story, and the strange logic of human choice than I expected it to.
          I started this journal because the world does not slow down long enough for most of us
          to sit with a question, and I wanted a place to do exactly that: to think in public,
          imperfectly, about what is changing and what, underneath all of it, remains. If there
          is one question this whole studio circles back to, it is this — what made us human, and
          what will it take to stay that way.
        </p>

      </div>

      <div class="about-photo">
        <img src="/bhavya-photo.jpg" alt="Portrait of Bhavya" />
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about-header {
    padding-top: 3rem;
    padding-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }

  .about-title {
    font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 5vw, 3.25rem);
  }

  .about-layout {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 3rem;
    padding-bottom: 5rem;
    align-items: start;
  }

  .about-content {
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }

  .about-content p {
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    line-height: 1.85;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
  }

  .about-photo img {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    display: block;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
  }

  @media (min-width: 900px) {
    .about-layout {
      grid-template-columns: 1.4fr 1fr;
    }

    .about-photo {
      max-width: 340px;
      justify-self: end;
    }
  }
</style>